# main-overview

## Development Guidelines

- Only modify code directly relevant to the specific request. Avoid changing unrelated functionality.
- Never replace code with placeholders like `# ... rest of the processing ...`. Always include complete code.
- Break problems into smaller steps. Think through each step separately before implementing.
- Always provide a complete PLAN with REASONING based on evidence from code and logs before making changes.
- Explain your OBSERVATIONS clearly, then provide REASONING to identify the exact issue. Add console logs when needed to gather more information.


CouchCMS Documentation implements a specialized knowledge hierarchy organized around domain-specific concepts and features:

Core Documentation Structure:
- Getting Started
- Core Concepts
- Tags Reference
- Add-Ons
- Tutorials by complexity

Domain Features:
1. Template Management
   - Sub-Templates (New Feature)
   - Template Inheritance (New Feature)
   - Core tag implementations

2. Custom Routing System
   - Extended routing capabilities
   - Custom route definitions
   - URL management

3. Entity Framework
   - Extended Entities (New Feature)
   - Entity relationships
   - Custom data models

Components containing business logic are organized into presentation layers for media content and documentation structure, with specific focus on CMS-specific implementations and content organization patterns.

Importance Score: 75 - Represents key documentation organization for core CMS functionality

